// Byakugan risk gate — PROBE (informational, not gated): what the NAIVE join
// shape — the contract's reference query, no stash/restore — does to the two
// source fields the lookup index also maps but must not change. The runner
// reads the result and reports, per flagged line:
//   @timestamp          evidence time (2019) kept, or replaced by the lookup
//                       row's @timestamp (the detection time, 2026)?
//   process.entity_id   on the Security.evtx file line, whose lookup row has NO
//                       process.entity_id: owner link kept, or nulled?
// The answer on this cluster decides whether every joining query needs the
// stash/restore of 20-lookup-join-flag.esql, or only the writer needs to stop
// setting @timestamp on lookup rows (docs/riskgate.md, "if it fails").
FROM logs-car.*-riskgate METADATA _id, _index, _version
| LOOKUP JOIN car-detections-riskgate ON event.id
| WHERE detection.id IS NOT NULL
| KEEP event.id, car.object, @timestamp, process.entity_id, detection.id, detection.detected_at
| SORT event.id ASC, detection.id ASC
| LIMIT 100
